6186: # The seats of a routed panel (D1, D4): $Candidates (roster order) of { Position; Lab; Weight;
6187: # Pinned }; $K seats. Pinned candidates take the first seats (rule `required`, roster order); then
6188: # the lab reserve (wave 26b, D5 / F22-5 - defined over the seats LEFT after the pins): reserve =
6189: # min(K - the pinned, the labs with a candidate weighing >= $Neutral that the pins did not seat);
6190: # while fewer reserve seats than that are taken, the draw is restricted to candidates of a lab not
6191: # yet seated that weigh >= $Neutral (rule lab-draw / lab-explore); otherwise it draws from every
6192: # candidate left (rank-draw / rank-explore). (The same seats as the wave 26 formulation min(K,
6193: # good labs) over all seated labs - D5 changed the statement, not the draw.) A slot explores (a
6194: # uniform pick from the same pool) when its second
6195: # uniform is below $Explore; else the weighted pick: the first candidate, in roster order, whose
6196: # running weight sum exceeds uniform x the pool's weight sum. The winner leaves the pool.
